      "message": "atlas (54-c): cap raised + fleet audit — true count 4848 (49 pages, Link-follow, cap 120 not hit)\n\nCAP RAISE: pagination follows Link headers (rel=next) until exhausted,\nbounded by a 120-page hard safety cap; pages_fetched/pagination_cap/\npagination_cap_hit receipted in atlas.json. Old 40-page cap pinned the\nmap at exactly 4000; true account count is 4848 (independently confirmed\nby rel=last page 4848 at per_page=1).\n\nSTABILITY (audit rule): all 4000 previously-classified repos keep family,\nstage and matched keywords byte-identical — drift = 0, lost = 0; 848 new\nrepos added (fleet 154, other 322, quilt 17, qthe 344, latent 2, jev 5,\nmoth 4). One upstream metadata change receipted: MicroMoth-quilt language\nC#->Python (classification evidence untouched).\n\nFLEET AUDIT: deterministic 30-of-1153 sample of desc-stage fleet repos\nread by hand — 25/30 genuinely fleet (83% strict; 27/30 with defensible\nmulti-agent-theory borderlines) >= 70% bar, synonym table KEPT; 53-e\nhoover suspicion refuted on this account (surface: agent=844, fleet=425,\ncrab=9, lane=6, receipt=6, seeds=2). Misses receipted: lau-compilers\n('agent DSL' tail-match), superinstance-embedder ('Seeds' as verb).\nQueued (next lane): qthe synonym audit — desc 83->427 with new pages,\n'canon' matches adjective 'canonical' (substrate-opposites).\n\nFamilies now: other=2502 fleet=1555 quilt=246 qthe=460 jev=44 moth=23\nlatent=18. Env-gated ATLAS_DUMP audit lane added to the builder.",
